    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.layout_spectral - Edgecase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.layout_spectral.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_spectral()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Place the nodes using eigenvectors of the graph Laplacian.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_spectral()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: Place the nodes using eigenvectors of the graph Laplacian.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.layout_spectral()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Place the nodes using eigenvectors of the graph Laplacian.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nPlace the nodes using eigenvectors of the graph Laplacian.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L5597-L5685){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.layout_spectral(\n    weighted=None,\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Spectral layout](../assets/graphs/layout-spectral.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, a three-by-three grid graph scattered at random. On the right, layout_spectral() places the nodes by two eigenvectors of the graph's Laplacian, which recovers the grid: nine nodes in three rows of three, joined to their neighbors.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe coordinates of each node are its entries in the eigenvectors of the second and\nthird smallest eigenvalues of the Laplacian `L = D - A`. These vectors are the\nsmoothest non-constant functions on the graph, so adjacent nodes get similar\ncoordinates: the layout shows the global shape (rings, grids, the two halves of a\nbarbell) cleanly, but it can crowd dense regions into a small area. The result is\ncentered and scaled so the largest coordinate is `scale=`. This matches NetworkX's\n`spectral_layout()`, up to the sign of each axis, which is fixed here so that the\nfirst node with a nonzero coordinate has a positive one.\n\nEdge direction is ignored (directed graphs use `A + A^T`), parallel edges add up and\nself-loops are skipped. A disconnected graph has several zero eigenvalues, so its\ncomponents collapse onto a few points; lay out components separately or use a\nforce-directed layout instead. Graphs of 400 nodes and more use a sparse eigensolver.\nGraphs with one or two nodes have no third eigenvector: one node goes to `center=`,\ntwo nodes to either side of it.\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[bool]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, use edge weights (`1` where missing) as adjacency entries. If `False`,\n    every edge counts `1`. If `None` (default), follows whether the graph was created\n    as weighted.\n\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Largest coordinate after rescaling. `None` keeps the raw eigenvector entries\n    (`center=` is then ignored). Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the layout, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `weighted=True` and an edge weight is negative or not finite, or `scale=` or\n    `center=` is invalid.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA grid comes out as a grid:\n\n::: {#2ffb4f62 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nec.Graph().add_grid_graph([6, 6]).layout_spectral().plot(layout=\"pos\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"7.3 15.2 685.4 489.6\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"7.3\" y=\"15.2\" width=\"685.4\" height=\"489.6\" fill=\"#fafafa\"/>\n<line x1=\"309.1\" y1=\"241.4\" x2=\"337.7\" y2=\"210.0\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8399999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-16-0\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"310.0\" y1=\"262.3\" x2=\"341.4\" y2=\"290.9\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8399999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-21-1\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"289.1\" y1=\"263.2\" x2=\"267.0\" y2=\"287.5\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8399999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-28-2\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"288.2\" y1=\"242.3\" x2=\"263.9\" y2=\"220.2\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8399999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-23-3\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"478.2\" y1=\"184.9\" x2=\"502.5\" y2=\"207.1\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8399999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-2-4\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"457.3\" y1=\"185.9\" x2=\"453.0\" y2=\"190.7\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8399999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"3-9-5\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"456.4\" y1=\"165.0\" x2=\"425.0\" y2=\"136.3\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\